\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. LIGHT of the world, faint were our weary feet
\par With wandering far;
\par But Thou didst come our lonely hearts to greet,
\par O Morning star;
\par And Thou didst bid us lift our gaze on high,
\par To see the glory of the glowing sky.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In days long past we missed our homeward way;
\par We could not see;
\par Blind were aur eyes, our feet were bound to stray:
\par How blind to Thee!
\par But Thou didst pity, Lord, our gloomy plight;
\par And Thou didst touch our eyes, and give them sight.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Now hallelujah rise along the road
\par Our glad feet tread;
\par Thy love hath shared our sorrow's heavy load;
\par There's  light o'erhead:
\par Glory to Thee whose love hath led us on,
\par Glory for all the great things Thou hast done.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Where is death's sting, where, grave, thy victory,
\par Where all the pain,
\par Now that Thy King the veil that hung o'er thee
\par Hath rent in twain?
\par Light of the world, we hear Thee bid us come
\par To light and love in Thine eternal home.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

